[00:19.10]1. There is a book that by its many pages,
[00:24.10]Brings peace and joy and hope to humankind.
[00:30.10]Its wondrous thoughts are charged with such great power;
[00:37.05]It brings life to the “dead,” sight to the “blind.”
[00:42.69]That precious book is God’s own Holy Bible.
[00:48.76]Its words were penned by men whom God inspired,
[00:54.92]By men who truly loved their God Jehovah,
[01:00.96]And by his holy spirit they were fired.
[01:23.32]2. They wrote a record true of God’s creations,
[01:29.32]How by his might this universe appeared.
[01:35.32]They also told how man at first was sinless
[01:41.32]But how his Paradise then disappeared.
[01:48.00]They further told about a certain angel
[01:54.24]Who challenged God and spurned his sov’reignty.
[02:00.32]That challenge led to sin and man’s great sorrow,
[02:06.64]But soon will come Jehovah’s victory.
[02:25.34]3. The time has come with reason for rejoicing:
[02:30.94]Jehovah rules by his anointed King.
[02:37.34]So now we preach the good news of the Kingdom
[02:44.06]And share the hope of blessings it will bring.
[02:49.06]Within his book are found these cheerful tidings;
[02:55.58]A sacred banquet feast on which to feed.
[02:58.54]It offers peace beyond all human thinking;
[03:00.43]This Living Treasure beckons all to read.